  "Name": "Young1961-T2-n150-W100-k4",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Synthesis of multiple antireflection films over a prescribed frequency band,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 51, 967-974 (1961). doi:10.1364/JOSA.51.000967 - Table II p. 973 (W = 1.00, n = 1.50, k = 4: n1 = 1.04898, n2 = 1.15394) and Eq. (31)",
  "Notes": "Table II Tschebyscheff 4-layer AR coating from air to n = 1.50, W = 1.00.\nSpecification: Equiripple minimum of maximum reflection over W = 1.00.\nReported: Table I (k = 4, n = 1.50, W = 1.00): max amplitude reflection coefficient 0.01. Exact from Eq. (7): 0.0120 (R_max = 1.4e-4). R = 0.04 at 275 nm.\nNotes: As Young1961-T2-n150-W060-k2; n3, n4 from Eq. (31).\nLayers from Table II p. 973 (W = 1.00, n = 1.50, k = 4: n1 = 1.04898, n2 = 1.15394) and Eq. (31); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours max |r| 0.0120 from 367 to 1100 nm; paper max |r| 0.01 (Table I).",
